A) The theory is plausible but incomplete — temperature could contribute somewhat, but the more likely root cause is that the tool conflates a safe read and a mutating write behind one call with no structural separation. Fix: split into `get_ticket` (read-only) and `update_ticket_status` (mutation) — this removes the ambiguity regardless of temperature.
B) The engineer is correct — reverting to temperature 0 fully and reliably resolves the issue; no tool redesign needed.
